      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "State APR San Bruno: Table A 2022 lists Crestmoor High School, 300 Piedmont Ave, APN 019-170-020, application 2022-08-23, 155 units (8 low, 16 moderate deed-restricted, 131 above moderate), note 'Disposed former school site'. Table A2 2024 lists Crestmoor Project, entitled 2024-05-28, 155 units, 55-year term, density bonus with 3 other incentives, note 'SB330 Application'.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001129",
        "SRC-001123"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "May 2022 SummerHill fact sheet: 156 for-sale single-family detached homes on the 40.2-acre former Crestmoor and Peninsula High Schools site owned by SMUHSD, 132 market rate and 24 below-market (8 low-income at 80% AMI, 16 moderate at 120% AMI), all BMR homes 4-bedroom; about 24 acres developable, about 12 acres of open space to be dedicated to the city, 8 acres private open space; zoning R-1, proposed density 3.9 units/acre.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002772"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City Crestmoor fields page: SMUHSD owned the 40-acre parcel at 300 Piedmont Ave and has an agreement with SummerHill Homes LLC for its sale; SummerHill received city approval in June 2024 for a subdivision with 6.91 acres dedicated to the city (5.3 acres of fields, 1.61 acres of recreation and parking).",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002773"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Toll Brothers markets Crestmoor Estates at Courtland Dr and Piedmont Ave (sales center 183 Courtland Dr): Montara Collection 2,304-2,398 sq ft from $2,099,995 and Solara Collection 2,666-2,818 sq ft from $2,327,995; 4 bedrooms, 3 baths, loft. The Toll Brothers pages do not state a home count or mention SummerHill.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002774",
        "SRC-002776",
        "SRC-002775"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "County parcel layer: owner of record of 018-072-160 (300 Piedmont Ave) is 300 Piedmont Avenue LLC.",
